{"id":"tegami-mqrrtp7a","createdAt":"2026-06-24T07:47:52.918Z","version":"0.0.0","changelogs":{"google-fonts-typed-families.md":{"filename":"google-fonts-typed-families.md","content":"---\npackages:\n  npm:@takumi-rs/helpers:\n    type: minor\n---\n\n### Type `googleFonts` families against the Google Fonts catalog\n\n`GoogleFontFamily` now knows every Google Font, so known families autocomplete\ntheir available `weight`, `style`, and variable `axes`. Any other string still\npasses, keeping private or brand-new families working.\n\nSet a variable axis per family, e.g. `{ family: \"Inter\", axes: { opsz: \"14..32\" } }`.\nThe catalog is generated at build time and is types-only, so the runtime bundle is\nunchanged.\n"},"google-fonts-object-api.md":{"filename":"google-fonts-object-api.md","content":"---\npackages:\n  npm:@takumi-rs/helpers:\n    type: minor\n---\n\n### Subset Google Fonts inside `render`\n\n`googleFonts({ families })` returns every coverage subset of each family, with its\n`unicode-range`, a distinct name under one `subsetOf`, and a stable key. `render`\nregisters only the subsets the content draws, so a multilingual image pulls a\nhandful of blocks instead of whole fonts. Set `subset: false` to register\neverything; call `subsetFonts({ fonts, source })` to trim a set yourself.\n\nThis replaces `googleFont` and `googleFontSubsets` with one object-shaped\n`googleFonts`. Distinct subset names mean a glyph routes to the file that covers it\nrather than a same-named sibling that lacks it.\n"}},"packages":{"npm:@takumi-rs/wasm":{"type":"minor","bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"npm":{"distTag":"beta"},"publish":true},"npm:@takumi-rs/core":{"type":"minor","bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"npm":{"distTag":"beta"},"publish":true},"npm:@takumi-rs/helpers":{"type":"minor","changelogIds":["google-fonts-typed-families.md","google-fonts-object-api.md"],"bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"npm":{"distTag":"beta"},"publish":true},"npm:@takumi-rs/image-response":{"type":"minor","bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"npm":{"distTag":"beta"},"publish":true},"npm:takumi-js":{"type":"minor","bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"npm":{"distTag":"beta"},"publish":true},"cargo:takumi":{"type":"minor","bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs","sync \"takumi\" group package versions"],"publish":true},"cargo:takumi-wasm":{"publish":false},"cargo:takumi-raster":{"bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs"],"publish":true},"cargo:takumi-napi":{"publish":false},"cargo:takumi-css":{"bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs"],"publish":true},"cargo:takumi-svg":{"bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs"],"publish":true},"cargo:takumi-core":{"bumpReasons":["align with script-level configs"],"publish":true},"cargo:example":{"publish":false}}}